Tom: That''s brave of you, Mia. Aren''t you worried about the language?
Mia: A little. But I think it''s important to step outside my comfort zone.
Tom: True. What will you actually do there?
Mia: Mostly I''ll assist the nurses and help teach families how to stay healthy.
Tom: That sounds really rewarding. How long will you stay?
Mia: About six weeks. It takes time to be truly useful to a team.
Tom: Well, I think it''s a wonderful thing to do. Good luck!', '米娅报名暑假去另一个国家的儿童诊所做志愿者;汤姆担心语言问题;米娅觉得走出舒适区很重要;她主要协助护士、教家庭如何保持健康;要待大约六周,因为真正帮上团队需要时间;汤姆祝她好运。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What is Mia going to do this summer?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Volunteer at a children''s clinic abroad.","Open her own hospital.","Travel for a beach holiday.","Study at a local school."]},{"q":"What is Tom worried about for Mia?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["The cost of the flight.","The language she will face.","The weather there.","The food she will eat."]},{"q":"What will Mia mainly do at the clinic?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Assist the nurses and teach families.","Build new houses.","Sell medicine.","Drive an ambulance."]},{"q":"How long will Mia stay?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["About two days.","About six weeks.","About one year.","Only a weekend."]},{"q":"Why does Mia say she needs that much time?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Because flights are cheaper.","Because she likes long holidays.","Because being truly useful takes time.","Because the clinic is closed at first."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective2', 'U4', 'fltrp');
Its workers believe that medical care should cross every border.
They help people in danger, whatever country those people come from.
Those in the most serious danger are always treated first.
Today its members come from more than one hundred and fifty countries.', '一个名为''无国界医生''的组织多年前在巴黎成立;成员相信医疗援助应跨越一切边界;他们帮助处于危险中的人,无论来自哪个国家;最危急的人总是优先得到救治;如今其成员来自一百五十多个国家。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Where was the organisation founded?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["In London.","In Beijing.","In New York.","In Paris."]},{"q":"What do its workers believe?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Medical care should cross every border.","Only rich people deserve care.","Care should stay in one country.","Doctors should never travel."]},{"q":"Whom do they help?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Only people from one country.","People in danger from any country.","Only their own families.","Only famous people."]},{"q":"Who is treated first?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["The youngest people.","The richest people.","Those in the most serious danger.","The newest patients."]},{"q":"Where do its members come from today?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Only three cities.","Just one country.","Nowhere at all.","More than 150 countries."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective2', 'U4', 'fltrp');
Yuki: Honestly, the culture shock was bigger than I expected.
Ken: That''s normal. Everything feels new at first.
Yuki: Yes. But my classmates were so welcoming that I soon felt better.
Ken: It helps to stay open and curious, doesn''t it?
Yuki: Definitely. We share food from our home countries every Friday.
Ken: What a great idea! You learn from each other.
Yuki: Exactly. Now the world feels like one big village to me.', '肯问由纪在伦敦第一周怎么样;由纪坦言文化冲击比预想的大;肯说这很正常,起初一切都新鲜;由纪说同学很友好,她很快好起来;保持开放与好奇有帮助;他们每周五分享各自家乡的食物;互相学习;由纪觉得世界像一个大村庄。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"How did Yuki feel during her first week?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["The culture shock was bigger than expected.","She was completely bored.","She wanted to go straight home.","She felt nothing new at all."]},{"q":"What does Ken say about feeling that way?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["It means she should leave.","It is normal at first.","It will never get better.","It is her own fault."]},{"q":"Why did Yuki soon feel better?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Because the weather changed.","Because she stopped going to class.","Because her classmates were welcoming.","Because she found a new job."]},{"q":"What do they do every Friday?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Take a long flight.","Watch a football match.","Stay completely silent.","Share food from their home countries."]},{"q":"How does the world feel to Yuki now?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Like one big village.","Like a lonely place.","Like a closed door.","Like a boring town."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective2', 'U4', 'fltrp');
His speech lasted only about two minutes.
Yet his short words gave his divided people new hope.
He asked everyone to work towards the equality of all people.
Today that speech is still remembered as words that changed a nation.', '1863年,一位领袖站在许多士兵牺牲的战场上;他的演说只持续约两分钟;但简短的话语给分裂的人民带来新希望;他呼吁人人为所有人的平等而努力;如今这篇演说仍被铭记为改变了一个国家的话语。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Where did the leader give his speech?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["In a busy shopping street.","In a field where soldiers had died.","On a sandy beach.","Inside a small school."]},{"q":"How long did the speech last?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["A whole day.","Several hours.","Only about two minutes.","A full week."]},{"q":"What did his short words give the people?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["More fear.","Less courage.","A reason to fight on.","New hope."]},{"q":"What did he ask everyone to work towards?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["The equality of all people.","More division.","Personal wealth.","Greater fame."]},{"q":"How is the speech remembered today?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["As a forgotten failure.","As words that changed a nation.","As a funny joke.","As a list of names."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective2', 'U4', 'fltrp');
Ben: Great. I think every class should present a different country.
Anna: Good idea. It is important to make every student feel included.
Ben: Right. We could invite families to share their own traditions too.
Anna: That would be wonderful. Food, music and dance from everywhere.
Ben: It takes real teamwork to organise such a big event.
Anna: True, but I''m sure it will be rewarding for the whole school.
Ben: Let''s start sending out the invitations tomorrow.', '安娜提议一起筹划学校的国际文化日;本认为每个班级展示一个不同的国家;安娜说让每个学生都有参与感很重要;本建议邀请家庭来分享各自传统;来自各地的美食、音乐和舞蹈;本说办这么大的活动需要真正的团队协作;安娜相信对全校都很有意义;他们打算明天开始发邀请。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What are Anna and Ben planning?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["A maths exam.","A sports race.","An International Culture Day.","A class trip to the seaside."]},{"q":"What does Ben suggest each class should do?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Sell tickets.","Stay at home.","Write a long test.","Present a different country."]},{"q":"Why does Anna want every student to take part?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["To make everyone feel included.","To win a prize.","To save money.","To finish early."]},{"q":"What does Ben say is needed to organise the event?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["A lot of money.","Real teamwork.","Good weather.","Quiet classrooms."]},{"q":"What will they start doing tomorrow?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Cancelling the event.","Closing the school.","Sending out the invitations.","Taking a long holiday."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective2', 'U4', 'fltrp');
During a big match, fans from many countries cheer at the same moment.
Players shake hands and show respect, whoever wins the game.
People who share no common language can still enjoy the same goal.
In this way, sport helps to break down boundaries between strangers.', '体育有一种把人们聚到一起的特殊力量;一场大赛中,许多国家的球迷在同一刻欢呼;无论谁获胜,球员都握手致敬;没有共同语言的人也能一起为同一个进球喝彩;就这样,体育帮助打破陌生人之间的界限。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What special power does sport have?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["It keeps people apart.","It makes people angry.","It costs a lot of money.","It brings people together."]},{"q":"What do fans from many countries do during a big match?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["They cheer at the same moment.","They stay silent.","They leave at once.","They watch different games."]},{"q":"What do players do after the game?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["They argue loudly.","They shake hands and show respect.","They refuse to meet.","They blame the loser."]},{"q":"What can people without a common language still do?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Read the same book.","Speak the same words.","Enjoy the same goal.","Write the same essay."]},{"q":"What does sport help to break down?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["The rules of the game.","The players'' health.","The fans'' tickets.","Boundaries between strangers."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective2', 'U4', 'fltrp');

